ViewVEF 1.0 by Vaughn Cato

   ViewVEF is a small program that allows you to display "flicker VEF" files
as well as the normal vef files.  The command format is:

viewvef <filename> [<pause length>]

   If a file with the filename given and a .2 extension is found it will be
flickered along with the file with the filename.  If not, only the file with
the filename specified will be displayed.  If no pause length is specified,
it will pause until the ENTER key is pressed.  If a pause length is
specified, it will delay for that many seconds before ending.
